<main class="container mt-5 mb-5">
  <div class="row">
    <div class="offset-md-1 col-md-10">

      <h1><%= title %></h1>

      <h2>A Little About Me</h2>
      <p>
        I'm currently studying Networking and IT Security at Ontario Tech University. I've always enjoyed working with technology, and through my program, I've become especially interested in networking, cybersecurity, and how different systems work together. I like being able to take what I learn in class and actually apply it to projects.
      </p>

      <h2>Education and Technical Skills</h2>
      <p>
        Throughout my program, I've had the chance to work with different technologies, including Cisco Packet Tracer, AWS, Linux, and Visual Studio Code. I've learned about network configuration, operating systems, cloud computing, and troubleshooting, which has helped me better understand how IT systems work.
      </p>

      <p>
        I've also worked with programming languages such as Python, JavaScript, and C, along with HTML and CSS for web development. Some of my favourite assignments have been the ones where I get to build something myself, whether that's setting up a network, deploying cloud resources, or creating a website.
      </p>

      <h2>Leadership and Experience</h2>
      <p>
        Outside of school, I've worked for the Town of Aurora in several recreation positions, including as a Service Agreement Director for summer camps. This gave me the opportunity to lead activities, work with different groups of people, and take responsibility for making sure programs ran smoothly. It's helped me become more confident with communication, teamwork, and handling unexpected situations.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm also involved with student organizations at Ontario Tech, including being a Deputy Executive for the Networking and IT Security Society (NetSoc). Being involved on campus has been a great way to meet other students who share similar interests and continue building my leadership skills.
      </p>

      <h2>Looking Ahead</h2>
      <p>
        As I continue my studies, I'm looking forward to learning more about the IT industry and gaining hands-on experience. I'm especially interested in exploring opportunities in networking, cybersecurity, and IT infrastructure. My goal is to keep improving my skills and eventually put what I've learned to use in a professional environment.
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
</main>

